Z||000000||Bill 88||05-03-2001||01:51 PM|||| I think I have read about the 'carsearch' site or something close to that name.  It tells about the car's history.  Has anyone tried it and/or do I have the right name?||||reg||1
Z||000001||GoCartGuy||05-03-2001||02:04 PM||||Its called carfax.com  and its ok.  One thing that really bugged me is that you can run a quick search and they'll tell you if anything pops up in the database but to actually get the info that's in there you gotta fork over like $20.  I know it doesn't sound like much but they've got everything from sales to accidents in this database and all they tell you is how many mentions there are.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Database Nut||05-03-2001||02:06 PM||||Bill,<P>It's <A HREF="http://www.carfax.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carfax.com</A>     They run the VIN to check for records, and report how many they find to you, for free.  If you want to look at them then they charge you to do so.  Not a bad way to get the scoop on problems in the car's history.  I run the '88 Fiero Database,  and have info on around 2600 of them.  Maybe I have yours, from a previous owner?  Give me the last 5 digits of the VIN (After the ....JP2 part) and I'll check for you.<P>Good Luck,<P>John Willhoff<BR>88 Database Nut john.willhoff@lmco.com, BJWillhoff@aol.com, (770) 578-6556||||reg||14
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-03-2001||02:15 PM||||thats all they tell you for free. I signed up for the 2 months unlimited deal, and used it about 40 times while looking for the car I just bought.<P>  It acutally scared me away from an 88 formula w/110k that sold on ebay on easter morning for $1100. I didnt bid on the car because the carfax only reported one record, that the car had been sold at auction a year ago. In the ebay ad the seller said they got the car as a tradein, and it had the same mileage as carfax reported a year earlier.<P>  It also worried me that carfax only found one record, as if the car didnt exist before last year. But I have since discovered that records (like registration, title and inspection) from some states dont show up on carfax for some reason.<P>  So I think the carfax report may have scared me away from a good car, simply because i didnt understand what all the info meant at the time (or the lack of info).<P>  I did a check on a VW rabbit covertible on ebay that was listed as having 77k miles on it, from california. carfax found inspection and title records for the VIN number with mileage up to 220k miles! So the odo had been rolled back and whoever bought that car (it went for $1700) got totally screwed. <P>   Thanks to carfax, it wasnt me   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It also tells you which states the car has been registered in, so if some guy is saying the car is from arizona, and its been registered in vermont for 15 years...<P>if you are looking to buy a used car, it think its worth the $20. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill 88||05-03-2001||05:04 PM|||| Thanks everyone.  And John, I sent the number. Thanks if I forget to say it. This group has been a life saver a couple of times or at least a money saver for me.||||reg||1
